# Deployment scope for the Vercel project: Flutter Web sources only.
#
# Vercel does NOT honour .gitignore when collecting deployment files. Without
# this file every local build artefact is uploaded on each deploy — the source
# upload measured 11,831 files / 2,122 MB (975.9 MB compressed), of which
# build/, backend/ and .dart_tool/ accounted for ~2,111 MB.
#
# Everything the web build actually needs must stay OUT of this file:
#   lib/  web/  assets/  pubspec.yaml  pubspec.lock  analysis_options.yaml
#   .metadata  vercel.json  scripts/vercel-build.sh
#
# scripts/validate_vercelignore.py enforces both halves of that contract in CI.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local environment files. Vercel injects the real values from the project's
# environment settings at build time, so these must never ride along in the
# source upload. Vercel auto-ignores .env.local but NOT .env, which was being
# uploaded on every deploy before this rule.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .NET backend — built and deployed separately (Render), never by Vercel.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
backend/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local build output and tool caches. Vercel regenerates these from
# pubspec.lock via `flutter pub get --enforce-lockfile` + `flutter build web`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
.dart_tool/
.flutter-sdk/
coverage/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Non-web platform sources. Irrelevant to `flutter build web`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
android/
ios/
linux/
macos/
windows/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests — run in CI, not during the Vercel build.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
test/
integration_test/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation and CI configuration.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/
.github/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repo tooling not used by the web build.
# scripts/vercel-build.sh is deliberately NOT excluded — it is the buildCommand.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
scripts/ci/
scripts/tests/
scripts/__pycache__/
scripts/node_modules/
scripts/process_usda.py
scripts/scan_tracked_secrets.py
scripts/requirements-secret-scan.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local database files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
